    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n89983" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσποί-ημα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>that which one takes to oneself unduly, pretence,
				assumption</i> of a thing, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1127a20
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς καλοκἀγαθίας,
			δικαιοσύνης</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Heraclid.Pont.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				14.625a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.858f
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>deception, illusion</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				<u>Nat.</u>
				11.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>disguise</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν π. φίλων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					10.13
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>BC</u>
				3.64
			</span></i>.</div>
